# Casewell — the runnable request catalog.
#
# Open in VS Code (REST Client) or a JetBrains IDE and fire these at a running instance.
# Dev-auth headers mean there is no token setup. WHEN YOU ADD AN ENDPOINT, ADD ITS REQUEST HERE
# IN THE SAME PR.
#
# @base is the API's HTTP endpoint. Under the Aspire AppHost, read it off the dashboard resource
# `casewell-api`; under headless Mode B (see RUNBOOK.md §2) it is the --urls value below.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8094
@subject = dev-user
@tenant = dev
@roles = system_admin
@module = legal

### Liveness — never calls the LLM, safe to poll
GET {{base}}/alive

### Health — dependencies (DB) reachable
GET {{base}}/health

### Branding (anonymous — the only unauthenticated platform route)
GET {{base}}/api/platform/branding

### ─────────────────────────── Platform ───────────────────────────

### Modules + the tabs this caller can see. Must contain "legal".
GET {{base}}/api/platform/modules
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Who am I — user, tenant, effective permissions
GET {{base}}/api/platform/me
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Build / platform info
GET {{base}}/api/platform/info
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### ─────────────────────────── Chat over AG-UI ───────────────────────────

### A read-only turn. Streams RUN_STARTED → TOOL_CALL_* → TEXT_MESSAGE_* → CUSTOM(token_usage)
### → RUN_FINISHED. Any RUN_ERROR is a failure, never noise.
POST {{base}}/api/agui/{{module}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{
  "messages": [{ "id": "m1", "role": "user", "content": "List my matters" }]
}

### An approval-gated write. Emits CUSTOM(approval_required); the reply must NOT claim the write
### happened. Seed the matter first with the POST /api/legal/matters request below.
POST {{base}}/api/agui/{{module}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{
  "messages": [{ "id": "m1", "role": "user", "content": "Record a 5000 retainer deposit into trust on Acme Corp - NDA" }]
}

### Conversations
GET {{base}}/api/chat/conversations
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### ─────────────────────────── Approvals (human in the loop) ───────────────────────────

### Pending approvals — needs chat.approvals.manage
GET {{base}}/api/chat/approvals
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Approve one (paste an id from the list above) → { status: "Executed", result: "..." }
POST {{base}}/api/chat/approvals/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/approve
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{}

### Reject one → { status: "Rejected" }, and nothing is written
POST {{base}}/api/chat/approvals/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/reject
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{}

### ─────────────────────────── Admin (RBAC, audit, usage) ───────────────────────────

### Every tool + the permission gating it. After adding a tool this MUST list it — if it does not,
### the manifest and IModuleToolSource disagree and the tool will never be callable.
GET {{base}}/api/admin/security/catalog
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Append-only tool-call audit — every invocation, with its permission and outcome
GET {{base}}/api/admin/audit/tool-calls
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Roles
GET {{base}}/api/admin/roles
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Users
GET {{base}}/api/admin/users
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### RBAC negative check — a narrow role must be refused, not gated. Expect 403.
GET {{base}}/api/admin/security/catalog
X-Dev-Subject: outsider
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: guest

### ─────────────────────────── Legal module (the hand-edit surface) ───────────────────────────

### Matters
GET {{base}}/api/legal/matters
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Create a matter (legal.manage — a person on a form needs no approval gate; RBAC is the gate)
POST {{base}}/api/legal/matters
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{
  "name": "Acme Corp - NDA",
  "clientName": "Acme Corp",
  "practiceArea": "Corporate"
}

### Clients
GET {{base}}/api/legal/clients
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Calendar events
GET {{base}}/api/legal/events
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Tasks
GET {{base}}/api/legal/tasks
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Time entries (drives the Time tab)
GET {{base}}/api/legal/time-entries
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Weekly hours (drives the Hours tab)
GET {{base}}/api/legal/time/weekly
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Trust journal (drives the read-only Trust tab)
GET {{base}}/api/legal/trust-transactions
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Clause library
GET {{base}}/api/legal/clauses
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Contract-review playbook
GET {{base}}/api/legal/playbook
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}
